  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="39">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIIAtr">VIII Atr</ref> 39</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="39" corresp="#wit-d">And git mæg ðeah bot cuman, wille hit man georne on eornost aginnan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">And yet nevertheless improvement can come, if there is the zealous desire to begin it in earnest.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d">And yet improvement can still come, if one will begin it zealously and in earnest.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und doch kann wohl noch Besserung kommen, wolle man es [nur] eifrig im Ernste beginnen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And yet amendment may still come, if only it is eagerly begun in earnest.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
